  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-10-03T04:51:09.598Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I think it'd be nice if the camera was looked at and focused on a little some time, since the last update for cameras was I think literally when they released back in April or March of 2018. Nearly a year and a half later the camera is still basically the same as when it was first released.\n\nThere are a few issues with the current camera. For one, the buttons are still too hard to hit. This was admitted in the patch notes as a known problem when the camera was introduced. There's a canny that I opened up about that: https://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/camera-buttons-still-too-hard-to-hit\n\nSecondly, the camera lens is way too intrusive in the middle of your screen unless you place it somewhere. It would be nice if the camera lens could be above the screen instead of intrusively in the middle of it. These are my two main issues with the current camera.\n\nI think those issues are much more important to fix than adding new features, but new features for the camera would also be nice. Perhaps some kind of zoom function, longer delay option, button for a larger screen, etc. - a lot of people have good suggestions.",
